meta {
  name: Cancel an appointment you booked
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/appointments/:id/cancel
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id:
}

docs {
  Cancels a `held` or `confirmed` appointment and frees the slot immediately, so it
  shows up again in `GET /v1/practitioners/{id}/availability`. Only the booker can
  cancel (practitioner-side cancellation and rescheduling are a later story).

  Idempotent on an already-cancelled appointment (200).

  - 409 `HOLD_EXPIRED` — the hold had already lapsed; nothing to cancel.
  - 409 `CANCELLATION_WINDOW_CLOSED` — inside `APPOINTMENT_CANCEL_CUTOFF_HOURS`
    (unset locally, so cancellation is allowed any time before the start).
  - 404 — no such appointment booked by the caller.
}
